        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="0406" n="356" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg356"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Smythe to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States.</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince, Haiti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-05-15"><hi rendition="#italic">May 15,
                        1894</hi></date>.<lb/>(Received May 28.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 72.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * I have to inclose a copy of my note
                    to the foreign secretary in regard to the methods of levying tonnage dues, and
                    their evident discrimination against steam vessels. My note was almost identical
                    with that sent the same day by the consul-general of Great Britain, and I
                    believe the evil will be corrected.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry M. Smythe.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d353-a1.xml" xpointer="d353-a1"/>
